<title>CANADA: Canada signs flight deals in Central America.</title>
<headline>Canada signs flight deals in Central America.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's foreign affairs and transport ministers said in a joint statement that bilateral air traffic agreements had been reached with the Central American countries of Costa Rica, El Salvador, Guatemala and Nicaragua.</p>
<p>The pacts allow Canadian Airlines International Ltd, a unit of Canadian Airlines Corp, to operate air services to one city in each country, the statement issued late Thursday said.</p>
<p>&quot;The air services that will flow from the announcement will help support the government's efforts to develop relations with Central America, strengthen trade and boost tourism,&quot; said Foreign Affairs Minister Lloyd Axworthy.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
